sieve-filter-v2
; Loudness, which only the notes3 family has: every note between the softest and loudest levels
; allowed, and no jump in loudness between neighbouring notes of more than `step` levels, so a
; melody swells and fades rather than lurching. Rests are passed over. The state is the last
; note's level (0: none yet).
id        melody-loudness-notes3
version   1
author    Edward James Gordon (written with Claude)
origin    ai-directed
lines     audio
symbols   notes3*
describe  Notes between the softest and loudest levels, and no jump of more than the step between neighbours.
param     softest  int  1    1  127  the softest level allowed
param     loudest  int  127  1  127  the loudest level allowed (levels above the set's own are none)
param     step     int  2    0  126  the most the level may change from one note to the next

states    {LEVELS + 1}
start     0
accept    0..{LEVELS}
for n 1 {LONGEST}
  for from 0 {LEVELS}
    t {from} @{REST(n)} {from}
    for k {max(softest, 1)} {min(loudest, LEVELS)}
      if {from == 0 || abs(k - from) <= step}
        for p 1 {PITCHES}
          t {from} @{NOTE(p, k, n)} {k}
        done
      fi
    done
  done
done
end
